# the state of a handler is met anew from the blocks that stand under it, and with Handlers withheld it is empty. A read in the handler, or behind the place where it comes back, may find nothing noted of the list, so a loop that holds a handler block gets no row for its lists
# f1 = sumsUnderAHandler, f2 = Box
